{
  "dom_id": "step-e22088",
  "name": "Example: Computing a Unit Price With Conversion to Larger Units",
  "problem": "A bottle contains $32$ fluid ounces of juice and costs $\\[math]8.00.$ What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8\\mathbin{:}$  \n\n$$\n32 \\div 8 = 4\n$$\n\nSo, $32$ fluid ounces is the same as $4$ cups.  \n\nNow, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $4\\mathbin{:}$  \n\n$$\n8.00 \\div 4 = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the juice costs $\\[math]2.00$ per cup.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
